WEBVTT

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.980
<i>The sky is clear.</i>

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>I woke up exactly on time.</i>

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.740
<i>Temperature checks out okay.</i>

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.490
<i>No deviations from schedule.</i>

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.990
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.990
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:15.990
<i>Everything's perfect.</i>

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.490
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.490
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.300
<i>This... is Ryokushou!</i>

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:32.880
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:00.680
<b>Dancing in Autumn Colors</b>

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.680
Shouldn't the girl who's coming in 
for apprentice training be here soon?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.720
Yes.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.240
Nagomu! Take out the trash!

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.000
The garbage truck's coming at ten.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.520
Right away!

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.150
Nagomu-san!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.230
That hit perfectly in my solar plexus.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.040
What is it? What just happened?

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.630
I'm sorry. I was knocking, and I hit you.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.160
Knocking? I see!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.060
I'm here from Hachiten. I'm Kisaichi Hiiro.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.500
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.480
I-I'm looking forward to 
working with you, too.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.870
Oh, you're here?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.140
Fuki, look after her, would you?

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.850
I thought I'd have her sit out 
and observe the workshop today.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.260
No, I'm fine. I can jump in right away.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.470
Is that so?

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.630
Then show her to the changing room.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:50.270
Of course.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.200
She seems like a serious girl.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.650
I heard she completed confectionery 
school with outstanding grades.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.550
Was it that school over in Omiya?

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.490
That's what I heard.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.280
Perfect.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.800
<b>National Wagashi Competition</b>

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.800
<b>Sculpting and Construction Division</b>

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.800
<b>Artist: "Ryokushou" artisan</b>

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.760
This is made of sculpted sweets?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.780
That's right. It says the 
whole thing is made of sweets.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.890
It takes them months to make it.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.790
It's impressive, isn't it?

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.750
Wow...

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.480
It's so perfect!

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.050
<i>I get to train in the same place 
as the person I so admire.</i>

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.480
I look forward to your guidance!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.870
Yes, well... Nagomu!

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:51.410
Hm?

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.280
Start with teaching her how to clean.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.460
Are you sure? You're bringing her 
in as extra help, aren't you?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.690
We said she'd come to help, 
but it's also half for training.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.020
Her position is irrelevant.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.470
So...

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.840
The cleaning equipment is under the 
stairs behind this sliding door.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:10.810
Yes, sir!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.960
U-Um...

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.800
Oh, you can call me Nagomu.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.320
Calling me Irino would get confusing, right?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.320
<i>So he </i>is<i> the son of Ryokushou's 
master and mistress.</i>

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.220
<i>To think that someone of his 
standing would instruct me.</i>

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.120
But I never thought I'd get someone 
junior to me here so quickly.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.870
What? But I saw one young artisan...

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.970
Saki-kun?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.540
He's my senpai.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.410
I was in Tokyo doing different 
work up until this past spring,

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.860
so in terms of training, I'm about 
the same as you, Hiiro-chan.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.200
Then, did you come back with 
the intent to inherit the shop?

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.140
Oh, no. The successor's someone else.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:51.270
She's at school right now. 
I'll introduce you later.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.630
<i>Now, the equipment for cleaning up 
front is elsewhere, so...</i>

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:59.740
<i>Then he isn't the successor or anything, 
just a regular apprentice artisan,</i>

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.720
<i>and on the same career path as me.</i>

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:05.760
<i>No. Since I've spent two 
years learning the basics,</i>

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.110
<i>he has less experience than me?</i>

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.370
Who did this? Who sorted these adzuki?!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.200
I know who did it!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.710
How many times have I told you? 
You have to match the bean sizes!

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.460
Knock off that racket!

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.120
Oh, I did it again!

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.040
Don't waste flour!

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.400
<i>He makes too many mistakes. 
His work is incredibly sloppy.</i>

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.800
<i>How can he be so flawed?</i>

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.940
I'm back!

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.060
Welcome back.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.800
<i>Is she a new artisan here?</i>

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.070
How is Hiiro-chan working out?

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.200
I hear that lately, women are
 the ones with more grit.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.910
Well... they said that even at Hachiten, 
she was known as a serious girl.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.840
The way she notices things 
and takes action is exactly

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.370
what you'd expect from an honors student.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.090
It's just...

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:04.630
I get the feeling that she's working to make 
absolutely sure she shows no weaknesses.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.720
It reminds me of Itsuka 
when she first came here.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.540
I see.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.560
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.560
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:22.720
About the sweets for Tsukiyama-san's 
next tea party...

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.120
Oh, you mean those.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.140
We've had a request from the son.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.560
He said that he'd like cosmos as the theme.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.600
Well, it is autumn. I think that will be good.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:32.320
Nagomu?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.390
Will you go out on a delivery? 
It's within walking distance.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.450
Sure thing!

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.960
Traditional Confectionery
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.460
Oh, Nagomu-chan...

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.050
Are you on a delivery?

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.130
Is she new?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.220
That's right!

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.710
Be careful on your way!

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.200
Give my regards to the master of the shop.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.300
I will! Thank you!

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.640
Hello.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.280
You can be a little friendlier if you want.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.850
I don't know them.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.260
Well, no, but...

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:06.100
I believe there is no need 
to take pointless actions.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.990
<i>Really...</i>

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.510
<i>She's as hard as a rock.</i>

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.900
<i>I wonder if she's ever cracked.</i>

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.120
<i>But first...</i>

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.500
<i>That gaze she gives sometimes...</i>

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.000
<i>Is it really what I think 
it is, directed at Dad?</i>

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.500
<i>I mean, it's fine if it is.</i>

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.020
We've finished the delivery.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:33.760
In that case...

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.960
Will you go help out in the shop?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.640
<b>Fall Chestnut</b>

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.640
<b>Autumn Leaves</b>

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.640
<b>Wild Chrysanthemum</b>

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:36.820
Yes, sir.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.360
Our recommended sweets are...

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.590
I remember.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.400
Oh, right.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.200
<i>I will not do anything without purpose.</i>

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.400
<i>What I need...</i>

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.400
<i>is the path to perfection.</i>

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.710
Hello!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.020
Welcome!

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.510
Obachan! Thanks for earlier!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.250
<i>Earlier?</i>

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.260
After seeing your face, Nagomu-chan,

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.110
I got a craving for sweets.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:07.990
Well, thank you!

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.360
Now, let's see... I think...

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.280
Once you've decided, please let me know.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.140
Oh! I'm so sorry.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:22.980
I always ask Nagomu-chan, you see.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.110
If you wouldn't mind, Obachan, 
would you ask the artisan over there?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.270
Really? But she isn't very friendly.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.990
It's a little, you know...

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.320
<i>That would be... a crack forming, right?</i>

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.250
Excuse me!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:44.060
How may I help you?

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:46.650
I want to buy something for my friend.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:50.570
I'm going to Hokkaido tomorrow, but I don't
 know when we're going to meet up.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.760
<i>It's all right. I must do this perfectly.</i>

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.000
Um...

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.260
Y-Yes.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.740
If it's a gift, what do 
you think about this set?

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.020
But these are namagashi sweets, aren't they?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.140
I want something that will keep for days.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.420
Weren't you listening?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.570
How about yokan?

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.480
We have a seasonal item this month, 
yokan with chestnuts inside.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.490
I really love it!

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.030
Yokan? That might work!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.540
We can change the assortment in the set, too.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.490
<i>Even though...</i>

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.500
<i>a girl this young can do it...</i>

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.040
<i>I...</i>

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.430
A-Are you all right?

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:34.270
I am training to become 
a confectionery artisan.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.420
Doing something as pointless as interacting 
with customers is unnecessary.

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:44.320
Someone as flawed and frivolous 
as you need not worry for me.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:45.830
You're wrong!

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.110
It's true that Nagomu-san 
makes a lot of mistakes,

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.830
and that he's in no position 
to worry about others.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:58.270
But Nagomu-san cares for both the 
sweets and the customers equally.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.260
Itsuka...

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:00.570
That is not pointless!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.580
It's the most important thing!

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:05.200
I...

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.340
What is going on in this shop?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.380
Masa-san!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:15.960
No matter the reason, artisans arguing 
in front of the customers is inexcusable.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.240
It is not something you'll be praised for.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.480
I'm sorry.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.350
Good.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.640
I'll go cool off.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:37.030
<b>National Wagashi Competition
 Sculpting and Construction Division</b>

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:36.360
Our speaker today is...

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.690
an artisan from the traditional 
confectionery, Ryokushou,

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.620
<b>Special
Guest
Lecturer</b>

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.440
Tatsumi Masa-san.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.060
Pleased to meet you.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:48.040
<b>Artist: "Ryokushou" artisan
Tatsumi Masa</b>

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.040
<i>I've admired him for all this time.</i>

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.790
<b>Kyoto-style
\hConfectionery</b>

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.790
<b>Hachiten</b>

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.790
<b>Hachiten</b>

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:49.790
<i>One day...</i>

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:54.040
<i>I hoped to be able to train under him.</i>

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.340
<i>And yet...</i>

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.480
I...

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.120
I wanted to always be perfect.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.490
I thought there was nothing
 I couldn't accomplish.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.940
So, because didn't want to admit my faults...

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:29.880
I ended up speaking abusively.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.220
To be scolded like that at my age...

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.910
If there were a hole, I'd crawl into it.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.800
What's important...

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.780
is to make this experience count next time.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.610
No matter the person, 
everyone makes mistakes.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.920
If there is a perfect person,

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:54.590
that perfection is built through learning 
from the mistakes they've made.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:58.120
Me, all I do is make mistakes.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.280
But I feel better now.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:07.530
You've seemed steely and guarded 
since you were a student.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:11.220
I was worried you'd break.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.040
What?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:18.040
I remember you. You came and stared 
with such focus at what I was doing.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:24.300
You've done well to make it here 
to the world of wagashi.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.680
Take your time and enjoy it.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.060
I have a dream.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.810
I want to make sculpted sweets 
like the ones you make, Masa-san!

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:40.920
One day, when I'm able to make the 
kind of sweets you make, Masa-san...

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:44.070
When I can do that... will you praise me?

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.960
You'll have to be diligent.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.450
Yes, sir!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:13:00.800
<b>Dreams
for
the
Future</b>

00:12:56.450 --> 00:13:00.410
Very nice. Next, we have Irino Nagomu-kun.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:04.010
My dream is to work at a wagashi shop.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:08.940
Just like my grandpa and dad, 
I want to make delicious sweets.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:10.200
He's talking about a wagashi shop!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.690
That's so old-school!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.820
<b>Cooking Classroom</b>

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.320
<b>Ryokushou Presents!
Make and Eat
 Hands-On Wagashi Class!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.040
I've finished.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:27.980
Good.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.830
Excuse me for disturbing 
you while you're so busy.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.460
Principal! Welcome!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:35.660
Sensei!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.430
Nagomu-kun! My, you've gotten big!

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:42.130
Getting to see you in your work uniform 
like this is such a surprise!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.880
It was your dream to work 
in a wagashi shop, after all.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.790
Well, a lot happened...

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:51.890
But being able to settle down here like this,
 it's all thanks to your instruction.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.640
Please don't look at me 
with such utter disbelief!

00:13:55.640 --> 00:14:00.040
Sorry to ask so much of you today.
 Thank you for doing this.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:00.590
Of course.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:04.420
No problem. We're the ones who suggested it,
 so please don't let it bother you!

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.820
Then, until later.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.170
Whose fault do you think all of this is?!

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.160
Should I stuff anko in the 
cracks in your brain?!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.270
Anko should go in my mouth, please.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:20.790
How did this hands-on wagashi class 
come about in the first place?

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:24.200
The sweets for the tea ceremony 
classes they hold here...

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.040
We're always entrusted with making them.

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.470
But the other day, the tea 
ceremony teacher collapsed...

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.510
So we got a call canceling 
the order. That's when...

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.980
Then... what do you think of this?

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.510
Ryokushou presents...

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:42.310
<b>Ryokushou Presents!
Make and Eat
Hands-On Wagashi Class!

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:41.120
a make and eat, hands-on wagashi class!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.310
And that...

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.760
is how it happened.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.320
For crying out loud...

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.200
I see.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:50.520
Despite what he says, he made 
the handouts and things,

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:52.670
and he's been really looking forward to this.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:53.580
Wow...

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.350
What was that?

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.300
Nothing!

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.410
They're here!

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.590
Thank you for having us!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.430
Hello!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:03.040
Thank you for having us!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.750
Oh!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.510
Hey, Itsuka!

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:10.620
Oh, that's Itsuka's...

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:11.960
What should we call him?

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.350
You can just call him an old guy!

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:14.720
Moron!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.680
Can't you separate work 
from your private life?

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.240
<i>I came because he said he wasn't coming.</i>

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.990
<i>To think he can't even separate 
work from my private life.</i>

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.900
<b>6th Grade
Naruto Miyu</b>

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.910
First, please wash your hands.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.960
Make sure to use soap and 
wash up to your elbows.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:43.170
Once you've washed up, try not to 
touch your hair or anywhere else.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.860
You're so clumsy, honestly.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:48.980
Hurry and wash up.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.490
Everyone, hello.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.050
Hello!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:00.060
Today we'll be making two 
premier namagashi sweets.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:05.060
<b></b>• Greetings
 • Introduction of today's traditional sweets

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:05.060
We'll be making cosmos with nerikiri 
dough and momiji with kinton dough.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:09.060
Something pinker would have been better. 
Like a sakura flower or something.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.400
Now, a quiz!

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:14.410
Why are we doing cosmos and autumn maples?

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.320
Because it's fall!

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:17.410
Correct!

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.660
Wagashi express the seasons.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.720
For example, in spring, sakura blossoms...

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:25.420
In summer, goldfish...

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.910
In fall, momiji...

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.300
In winter, snow...

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.900
There are all kinds.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:36.160
They say that long ago, people would realize 
what season it was by looking at wagashi.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.420
That's how deeply wagashi 
is a part of everyday life.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.510
Interesting, right?

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:42.870
Anything's fine as long as it's yummy!

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.310
Well, that's true.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.940
The an we make is delicious. Don't worry.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.780
We'll pass it out now, so...

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.820
Oh! Don't eat it, okay?

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.950
We wouldn't do that!

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:01.040
So... we've pre-measured 
the an and dough for you.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.560
First, take the pale purple dough 
and roll it between your palms.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.620
Once you've rounded it, 
press a little and flatten it.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:10.830
Make the center a little thinner,

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.800
then place the white dough 
on top and spread it out.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:17.530
Place the an on top, then wrap it 
in the dough, keeping it round.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:21.310
When you turn it over, you'll see a 
hint of the white showing through.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.870
I don't see the white in mine.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.440
Itsuka-chan, you really are good at this!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.570
Do you practice at home?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:34.140
They let me use the leftovers, 
but I've still got a long way to go.

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:35.860
Really?

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:37.570
<i>Oh no.</i>

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.580
<i>It's not just the white, 
the anko is showing, too.</i>

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.220
How is it, Miyu? Did it work?

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:48.170
What is it? You could look like 
you're having a little more fun.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:51.400
Oh my! That's beautiful!

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:54.260
I'm good with my hands.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:57.460
<i>You're the only one having fun here.</i>

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.910
This stick is a triangular dowel.
 It's used for shaping.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.400
The heat of a person's hand

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:09.190
quickly dries out the wagashi, 
and will change its flavor, too.

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:13.530
Being able to shape it beautifully before 
that happens is what makes an artisan.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:17.530
Place the lines quickly, 
dividing it into eighths.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.030
Don't be timid. Press firmly.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:25.790
Use your fingers to pinch 
the sections and shape them.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.790
Add lines to the petal 
tips with a tap, tap, tap.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:33.800
Mark the center with the 
round stamping dowel.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:37.300
Place the yellow dough there...

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:41.850
and your premier namagashi sweet,
 Cosmos, is complete.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.930
Is this right?

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:47.420
You can press harder than 
you think. That's right.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.850
That's really good!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.150
Wow!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.540
Just what we'd expect from you!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.070
Miyu, did you finish yours?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.270
Hm? What's that?

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:00.170
That's not a cosmos!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.150
You really are so clumsy.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:06.730
U-Um...

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:10.460
I like it!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.260
I can tell you worked really hard to make it.

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:17.690
But... you can see the an inside.

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:20.220
Isn't it because you didn't want to do this?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:25.250
I thought it looked fun, so I wanted
 to do this together, but...

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:29.190
Mama... You always laugh at what I do.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.910
You made fun of me today too!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:36.170
Ever since I was little, you always laughed,
 no matter what I did.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.740
You made fun of me, saying I'm clumsy.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:41.990
Y-You've never once praised me!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.990
Miyu... I-It's not like that!

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.370
That's...

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.240
It's because you're so cute!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:55.130
Whether you'd messed up or 
were sulking... you were just so lovable.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.880
That's why I'd end up laughing.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:02.260
After all, I've been watching 
you since you were tiny.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.600
But ma'am,

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.140
she isn't a little girl anymore.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.940
When you get laughed at in a situation 
you don't think is funny...

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.990
It's so embarrassing.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.440
When I was in a situation like that...

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:20.240
Someone said this for my benefit.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.200
Laughing is rude!

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:27.500
Even if you don't intend to be mean, 
it can crush a person's potential!

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:30.310
<i>Nagomu-kun...</i>

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.650
An artisan must use the 
exact same proportions

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:39.090
to create the exact same 
shape in great quantity.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:43.110
That's so that every single customer 
can experience the same enjoyment.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:48.350
But it's something gained through training, 
repeating the same work over and over.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:51.430
The most important thing is to enjoy it.

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:55.440
What do you think, now that 
you've made wagashi? Is it hard?

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:00.790
It's hard, b-but it's fun.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.880
I'm glad.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.250
The next sweet is fun to make, too!

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:09.500
We'll take a strainer and 
press the dough through.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.830
Then we'll take chopsticks...

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.330
Thank you for the sweets!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.600
Miyu, I'm sorry.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.290
It's my fault, isn't it?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.150
There's something I forgot to tell you.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:29.470
Your mama...

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:33.110
loves your smile most of all!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:44.090
Nagomu-san, thank you for 
bringing me along today.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.110
No, thank you.

00:21:53.030 --> 00:21:55.220
What?

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:59.760
Then the person Hiiro-chan's 
been staring at is Masa-san?

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.500
I thought it was my dad!

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.710
No matter how you look at it, 
it's definitely Masa-san.

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:07.220
Though, more than love, 
I'd say it's admiration.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:08.990
Really?

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:11.370
Aren't you being a little too dense?

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:12.140
Oh!

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.720
Hey, Hiiro-chan, is the person 
you keep thinking about—

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:15.920
Nagomu-san!

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:16.860
What is it?

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:18.950
It's nothing!

00:23:50.110 --> 00:24:10.130
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:50.110 --> 00:24:10.130
<b>"Chestnut Retrospective"</b>

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:54.890
Now that I think about it, 
what brought you to Kyoto, Kanoko-san?

00:23:55.990 --> 00:23:58.540
Oh man! I feel all wobbly!

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.040
Welcome.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:06.420
He's been looking for something, 
but he can't find it.

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:09.720
What? That's magnificent! 
It's overflowing with dreams!
